{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/27124-trinity-era-novas","id":27124,"title":"Trinity Era Novas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T04:54:58-08:00","id":27124,"title":"Trinity Era Novas","content":"Will there be a few pages somewhere in the first few books on designing sane and stable Trinity Era Novas to fly around the Galaxy and do cool Sci Fi stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:00:18-08:00","id":27197,"title":"","content":"Just guessing here, but I'd imagine with the new carefully thought out rules systems you might be able to use Nova creation rules from the Aberrant book (assuming it covers Novas etc), and simply drop them into a Trinity game if the GM wanted to do that. <br /> <br /> That'd be a win-win really, no need to clutter up the Trinity book with stuff that takes away from Psions / Space-mad Abbies for GM's players not interesting in non-Psions in a Trin game (hi!). But those that want to drop Novas into other the other periods could do so with very little work from a systems perspective. That kind of flexibility could be very interesting actually across all settings. With the default being no work for a GM to simply keep their choice of setting 'clean'.<br /> <br /> I am really intrigued to see how Ian and co pull this off and allow for future new settings, all while building the new 'base' OPP system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:45:28-08:00","id":27351,"title":"","content":"I would think that the core rule book will tell us how to create PCs for all the eras. The era books will be specific with weapons, vehicles, and setting material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:09:44-08:00","id":27451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/27124-trinity-era-novas?p=27351#post27351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that the core rule book will tell us how to create PCs for all the eras. The era books will be specific with weapons, vehicles, and setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they might take a New World of Darkness approach and have the base rules be enough to run a certain kind of game -- the men and women of action hunting down strangeness as per the description of the core book -- and then each of the other line books will provide templates that you add on top of base characters, and those templates could be a Psion or an Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:52:02-08:00","id":27731,"title":"","content":"You could pretty easily design a Nova for Trinity with the old rules. Nothing stopped you. It was just that Aberrant's power scale is <i>dramatically</i> higher than Trinity's. I would imagine that will still be the situation in New Trinity. Aberrants/Novas are still gunna use the same system, they'll just be waaaay higher up the power level than Psions are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:46:01-08:00","id":27895,"title":"","content":"I just really wanted the cost of the Node Brain Merit and how many Nova points and Freebie points to assign the PCs. Second generation Novas and on would be a little different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T16:20:03-08:00","id":35186,"title":"","content":"The thought of Space Age Novas appeals to me. From Edenite Novas to other groups. I even tried to get a tainted Trinity-era Aberrant game going awhile back called; Aberrant Underground. Never got it off the ground though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}